course: dictionary
lesson: 15423
title: A stairway is a set of stairs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A stairway is a set of stairs. It can be inside a building, like the stairs in a house, or outside, like steps climbing up the side of a building. Its walls or the space around it often belong to it too.
explain: Use the words around a new word as clues. «The fire alarm rang, so we walked calmly down the stairway.» A fire alarm means danger, and people walk down stairs to get out, so a stairway must be a way out of a building. Swap in your meaning, and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: In a fire, never use the lift (elevator). Use the stairway instead. «The smoke was thick, so we all took the stairway.» When a word has a special safety meaning, your teacher will often tell you why it matters.
fact: A stairway is a set of stairs inside or outside a building.
fact: «The old stairway wound up the outside of the tower.» Here the stairway is outside.
fact: In a fire, use the stairway, not the lift (elevator).
fact: In stories and songs, «a stairway to the stars» can mean a path toward something wonderful.
fact: A good check for any new word is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «We ran down the stairway when the alarm rang.» What is a stairway? | A long, flat road | A small room at the top of a house | *A set of stairs in or on a building | A lift that carries people up and down
exercise: «The old stairway wound up the outside of the tower.» Where was the stairway? | Inside a teacup | In a shop window | Under the sea | *Outside the tower
exercise: There is a fire in the school. What should you use to get out of the building? | *The stairway | The roof | A lift (elevator) | Stay in your classroom and wait
test: «The song promised a stairway to the stars.» What does the stairway suggest here? | A pile of old bricks | A type of bird that sings | *A path toward something wonderful | Stairs made of ice
test: «He waited at the bottom of the stairway.» Where was he waiting? | *At the foot of a set of stairs | On the top of a hill | Up in the sky | Inside a lift
exam: Which is the best meaning of stairway? | A wall around a garden | A lift that carries people | *A set of stairs inside or outside a building | A narrow path through a forest
